{"seconds": 36.4, "exit": 0, "final": "Excellent! Black is up a bishop (material change +3). The move is **Bxf3**\u2014it's a deflection/decoy that forces White's bishop or pawn to capture on f3, leaving the g5 bishop undefended for Black's queen to capture.\n\n---\n\n**Coaching Note (\u226480 words):**\n\nWhen your opponent plays an attacking move like Bg5, don't panic\u2014look for how to turn the tables. Here, after Bxf3, White must recapture (either the bishop on e2 or pawn with gxf3), leaving the g5 bishop undefended. Your queen on the long diagonal can then grab it for free. The key: use a sacrifice to expose a defender and win material. Always check if an attacking piece has escaped route issues.\n\n---\n\n```json\n{\"move\": \"Bxf3\", \"line\": [\"Bxf3\", \"Bxf3\", \"Qxg5\"], \"motifs\": [\"deflection\", \"hangingPiece\"]}\n```", "tool_calls": [{"tool": "skill", "args": {"skill": "chess-coach"}}, {"tool": "chess-eyes-board", "args": {"fen": "rn2k2r/pp2bppp/2p1pn2/q5Bb/3P4/2N2N1P/PPP1BPP1/R2QR1K1 b kq - 1 10"}}, {"tool": "chess-eyes-threats", "args": {"fen": "rn2k2r/pp2bppp/2p1pn2/q5Bb/3P4/2N2N1P/PPP1BPP1/R2QR1K1 b kq - 1 10"}}, {"tool": "chess-eyes-line_view", "args": {"fen": "rn2k2r/pp2bppp/2p1pn2/q5Bb/3P4/2N2N1P/PPP1BPP1/R2QR1K1 b kq - 1 10", "square": "g5"}}, {"tool": "chess-eyes-line_view", "args": {"fen": "rn2k2r/pp2bppp/2p1pn2/q5Bb/3P4/2N2N1P/PPP1BPP1/R2QR1K1 b kq - 1 10", "square": "a5"}}, {"tool": "chess-eyes-line_view", "args": {"fen": "rn2k2r/pp2bppp/2p1pn2/q5Bb/3P4/2N2N1P/PPP1BPP1/R2QR1K1 b kq - 1 10", "square": "e1"}}, {"tool": "chess-eyes-line_view", "args": {"fen": "rn2k2r/pp2bppp/2p1pn2/q5Bb/3P4/2N2N1P/PPP1BPP1/R2QR1K1 b kq - 1 10", "square": "h5"}}, {"tool": "chess-eyes-line_view", "args": {"fen": "rn2k2r/pp2bppp/2p1pn2/q5Bb/3P4/2N2N1P/PPP1BPP1/R2QR1K1 b kq - 1 10", "square": "e7"}}, {"tool": "chess-eyes-line_view", "args": {"fen": "rn2k2r/pp2bppp/2p1pn2/q5Bb/3P4/2N2N1P/PPP1BPP1/R2QR1K1 b kq - 1 10", "square": "f3"}}, {"tool": "chess-eyes-leg